4,49.0,400.7,10.0,0.0,False,A. Age-Invariant Face Recognition
4,58.9,385.7,10.2,0.0,False,Early AIFR used discriminative subspaces [25]. Deep
4,49.0,373.8,9.8,0.026,False,methods decompose features into identity and age components
4,48.6,361.8,9.8,0.037,False,"(OE-CNN [6]), decorrelate them adversarially (DAL [7]), or add"
4,49.0,349.8,10.0,0.02,False,an ageing task (MTLFace [8]). AIM [9] couples an attention-
4,49.0,337.9,10.2,0.0,False,based synthesis network with disentangled representation
4,49.0,325.9,10.2,0.0,False,"learning, evaluates identity preservation with a user study"
4,49.0,314.0,10.1,0.0,False,"and recognition benchmarks (MORPH, CACD-VS, FG-NET,"
4,49.0,302.0,10.2,0.0,False,"IJB-C), and introduces the CAFR benchmark. OrdCon [10]"
4,49.0,290.1,10.2,0.057,False,contrasts direction vectors between features of younger and
4,49.0,278.1,10.2,0.057,False,older faces with the ageing direction and adds a soft proxy-
4,49.0,266.2,9.8,0.067,False,matching loss; it reports homogeneous and cross-dataset results
4,49.0,254.2,10.2,0.0,False,"on MORPH, FG-NET, and AgeDB and openly notes where"
4,49.0,242.2,9.8,0.045,False,dataset-specific methods outperform it. These methods change
4,49.0,230.3,9.8,0.044,False,the representation; AAFV-Net keeps the representations frozen
4,49.0,218.3,9.8,0.045,False,and changes the decision. The two are complementary: an AIFR
4,49.0,206.4,9.8,0.0,False,"embedding could replace ArcFace inside AAFV-Net, which we"
4,49.0,194.4,9.8,0.0,False,"have not tested. Large-margin matchers such as CosFace [26],"
4,48.6,182.5,10.2,0.0,False,"ArcFace [27], MagFace [28], and AdaFace [29] remain the"
4,49.0,170.5,10.0,0.015,False,strongest generic baselines; only ArcFace is evaluated here.
4,49.0,144.8,10.0,0.0,False,B. Face Age Progression and Identity Preservation
4,58.9,129.8,10.2,0.623,True,Conditional generators progressed from CAAE [30] and
4,49.0,117.8,10.2,0.709,True,"IPCGANs [31] to PFA-GAN [32] and SAM [33], which"
4,49.0,105.9,10.2,0.575,True,regresses StyleGAN2 [34] latent codes towards a target age.
4,49.0,93.9,9.9,0.499,False,"Generators can alter identity, particularly for large changes or"
4,48.7,82.0,9.8,0.528,True,young children [4]. AIM measures this with a user study [9]. We
4,49.0,70.0,9.8,0.479,False,use SAM unchanged and treat its outputs as noisy evidence; we
4,49.0,58.1,9.9,0.528,True,have not yet measured identity preservation with a recognizer
4,49.0,46.1,10.0,0.55,True,outside the pipeline (Section IX).
4,312.0,727.6,10.0,0.0,False,"C. Score Fusion, Quality, and Uncertainty"
4,321.9,712.6,10.2,0.556,True,"Classical fusion combines matcher scores by fixed rules,"
4,312.0,700.6,9.9,0.496,False,"density ratios, or learned classifiers [21]–[23]. Poh"
4,312.0,700.6,9.9,0.633,True,et al.
4,522.2,700.6,9.9,0.0,False,[24]
4,312.0,688.6,9.8,0.0,False,benchmarked quality-dependent and cost-sensitive fusion with
4,312.0,676.7,10.2,0.0,False,"missing modalities, which is the closest precedent for our"
4,312.0,664.7,9.8,0.0,False,reliability-weighted auxiliary branch. Probabilistic and quality-
4,312.0,652.8,10.2,0.0,False,"aware embeddings model per-sample uncertainty [28], [29],"
4,312.0,640.8,10.2,0.489,False,"[35], [36]. Our fusion is a small learned combiner of this"
4,312.0,628.9,9.9,0.456,False,family; its distinguishing element is that one input channel is
4,312.0,616.9,10.0,0.499,False,synthetic and is gated by an explicit reliability score.
4,312.0,590.7,10.0,0.0,False,D. Calibration
4,321.9,575.7,9.9,0.512,True,"Platt scaling [37], isotonic regression [38], and temperature"
4,312.0,563.7,10.2,0.581,True,"scaling [39] map scores to probabilities; ECE [40], Brier"
4,312.0,551.8,10.2,0.586,True,"score [41], and negative log-likelihood measure the result."
4,311.6,539.8,9.8,0.59,True,Xu
4,311.6,539.8,9.8,0.655,True,et al.
4,326.5,539.8,9.8,0.516,True,[42] calibrate face and kinship verification scores. All
4,312.0,527.9,9.8,0.0,False,of these are monotone maps; a threshold on a calibrated score
4,312.0,515.9,10.1,0.0,False,is a threshold on the raw score. This observation determines
