4,312.0,465.8,10.0,0.523,True,"E. Reject Option, Selective Classification, and Risk Control"
4,321.9,450.8,10.0,0.58,True,Chow derived the optimal error–reject trade-off for known
4,312.0,438.8,9.8,0.52,True,posteriors [11]; later work studies learning with rejection [12]
4,312.0,426.8,10.2,0.57,True,and selective deep classifiers with risk–coverage guaran-
4,312.0,414.9,9.8,0.558,True,"tees [13], [14]. Split-conformal methods and their risk-control"
4,312.0,402.9,10.2,0.51,True,extensions provide finite-sample guarantees under exchange-
4,312.0,391.0,9.8,0.562,True,"ability [15]–[17], with weighted variants for covariate shift [43]."
4,312.0,379.0,9.8,0.53,True,Our accept rule is a special case of this machinery (a maximum
4,312.0,367.1,9.8,0.51,True,"order statistic), and our reject rule is a conformal-style quantile;"
4,311.6,355.1,10.0,0.561,True,we use these results rather than claim them.
