9,49.0,241.0,10.0,0.0,False,C. Operational Workload
9,58.9,225.4,10.2,0.578,True,"Because genuine transactions dominate real streams, the"
9,49.0,213.5,10.2,0.529,True,review rate is driven mainly by genuine pairs. Table VIII
9,49.0,201.5,9.8,0.514,True,"converts the Look-2 rates into outcomes per 10,000 transactions."
9,48.5,189.6,9.8,0.627,True,"With 1% impostors, AAFV-Net sends about 2,970 transactions"
9,49.0,177.6,10.2,0.58,True,"to review against about 970 for guarded ArcFace, roughly"
9,49.0,165.7,9.8,0.579,True,three times the human workload. This holds whether impostors
9,49.0,153.7,9.9,0.589,True,are random or all ArcFace-mined. AAFV-Net produces fewer
9,49.0,141.8,9.8,0.532,True,genuine false rejects (54 versus 115). Its hard-impostor advan-
9,49.0,129.8,9.8,0.55,True,"tage converts look-alikes from review into automatic rejection,"
9,48.6,117.8,10.2,0.54,True,which matters only where look-alike attempts are frequent.
9,49.0,105.9,10.0,0.577,True,Removing the shared-target comparisons (No Shared Targets)
9,49.0,93.9,9.8,0.554,True,"halves the review load (1,615) while keeping zero random and"
9,49.0,82.0,9.8,0.55,True,"zero hard false accepts at test. On MORPH, therefore, the full"
9,49.0,70.0,10.2,0.485,False,system is not the best operating point among the evaluated
9,48.7,58.1,9.8,0.537,True,variants. We keep it as the primary system only because it was
9,49.0,46.1,10.0,0.547,True,designated in advance.
9,312.0,589.3,10.0,0.0,False,D. Age-Gap Analysis
9,321.9,574.2,10.2,0.513,True,Table IX shows that ArcFace accepts more genuine pairs
9,312.0,562.2,10.2,0.621,True,than AAFV-Net in G1–G3 (by 19.5–23.7 percentage points)
9,312.0,550.3,10.2,0.505,True,and that both collapse in G4–G5. Most of the deficit arises
9,312.0,538.3,10.2,0.423,False,in the guards rather than in the fused score. On the Look-
9,311.2,526.4,10.2,0.0,False,"1 test outputs, 97.38% of genuine pairs exceed"
9,311.2,526.4,10.2,0.0,False,T
9,523.0,524.9,7.0,0.0,False,acc
9,523.0,524.9,10.0,0.0,False,before
9,312.0,514.4,10.0,0.0,False,the guards are applied and 79.74% after (Fig. 3c). ArcFace’s
9,312.0,502.5,10.1,0.0,False,own guards cost about 4 pp (93.58% without versus 89.45%
9,311.6,490.5,10.2,0.0,False,with). The guards that make a zero-false-accept threshold
9,312.0,478.6,9.8,0.0,False,attainable (Section VII-H) therefore also remove many genuine
9,312.0,466.6,10.2,0.0,False,"pairs, a direct cost of the design that a better-targeted guard"
9,312.0,454.6,9.9,0.0,False,"might reduce. G4–G6 together contain 224 test pairs, and the"
9,312.0,442.7,9.8,0.0,False,"training split contains few long-gap genuine pairs, so long-gap"
9,312.0,430.7,9.8,0.0,False,behaviour on MORPH is essentially unmeasured. Without risk–
9,312.0,418.8,10.2,0.0,False,"coverage curves for both methods at matched FAR, which"
9,312.0,406.8,10.2,0.0,False,"require per-pair ArcFace scores that were not logged, we"
9,312.0,394.9,9.8,0.0,False,cannot claim improved cross-age verification on MORPH. The
9,312.0,382.9,10.0,0.0,False,evidence points the other way.
